<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pyramid of Djoser</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">27th century BCE</span> · Also known as Step Pyramid of Djoser</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pyramid of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/djoser">Djoser</a>, or Step Pyramid, is a six-stepped stone pyramid at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saqqara">Saqqara</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, built for the Third Dynasty king Djoser in the 27th century BCE. Attributed to his official <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imhotep">Imhotep</a>, it began as a mastaba tomb and was enlarged in stages, and it is regarded as the earliest large cut-stone building. It stands within a walled complex of courts and ceremonial buildings.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pyramid-of-djoser.jpg" alt="Pyramid of Djoser" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Olaf Tausch · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sakkara_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
